}
```

### SecurityBehavior ###

The **SecurityBehavior** (in the `security` module) adds access-control capabilities to a Model. It relies on a **Securable** data class to store security metadata such as permission names.


```java
@RegistrationPoint(exclusive = true)
public interface SecurityBehavior extends Behavior<Securable, Model> {

}
```


```java
@Register(value = SecurityBehavior.class, priority = PriorityLevel.Normal)
public class SecurityBehaviorImpl extends AbstractBehavior<Securable, Model> implements SecurityBehavior {

    @Override
    public void initBehavior() {
        // check permissions, listen security waves, etc.
    }

    @Override
    protected void initInnerComponents() {
    }
}
```

- `Securable` data carries permission metadata attached to the host Model.
- `initBehavior()` — enforce access rules or register security-related wave listeners.


    
